<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 55,388 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 55,388 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 55,388 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 43,991 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 5,989	    2,042</p>
<p>    Import cargo			49,399	   41,949</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and one berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and 14 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,500	 Arad		  7/10</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,300	 Wawasan Megah     4/10</p>
<p>Lube oil		  1,300	 Nagayevo	    6/10</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,534	 Johar		 8/10</p>
<p>Sugar		    14,000	 Azovlloyed	  8/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    58,400	 Kanpolis	    8/10</p>
<p>Feul oil		 42,000	 Probo Hawk	 11/10</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
